iolet which sold for  $14,000 and the rolls-royce Corniche  convertible for $180,000 so you can  guess which model ensured the  four-seater convertible survived  rolls-royce sold 3,000 cars in total  while VW sold 20,000 convertibles a year  fahncy thousand Paul Yong  after more than 20 years of production  the Beetle Cabriolet finally reached its  zenith in the 1303 robust reliable  equipped with a modern suspension and  capable of a top speed of 130 km/h and  yet the Beatles days were numbered  dhanyavad for years the soft-top beetle  was considered the world's best-selling  convertible during 31 years of  production over 330 thousand vehicles  rolled off the assembly lines only in  1991 was it overtaken by the VW Golf  when it was announced in 1978 that  production of the Beetle Cabriolet was  to end fans stormed the VW dealers to  snap up the last remaining cars which is  pretty rare in the fast-moving  automotive industry so the VW  convertible is definitely a milestone in  automotive history driving with the wind  in your hair the Beetle Cabriolet proved  convertibles don't have to be an  unaffordable luxury and in so doing has  guaranteed that the soft-top  lives on  you
 

